      "html": "<h3>Are daily van walkaround checks a legal duty in the UK?</h3><p>For the commercial vehicles the DVSA guide covers, yes: it says a walkaround check must be done every day. For vans it depends on your fleet, but driving a vehicle in a dangerous condition is an offence under section 40A of the Road Traffic Act 1988. The record is the proof.</p><h3>What does DVSA ask for in a fleet inspection?</h3><p>Records of daily walkaround checks, defect reports, and proof you acted. The DVSA guide says safety inspection records and driver defect reports must be kept for at least 15 months. Records must show who checked, when, what was found and what was done.</p><h3>Why do drivers stop using van check apps?</h3><p>Logins, updates and unfamiliar screens add time to a task they already dislike. A check takes 3 minutes. If opening the app takes 2, they skip it. WhatsApp is already open.</p><h3>How long should van check records be kept?</h3><p>The DVSA guide says at least 15 months for the commercial vehicles it covers. Keeping 15 months of digital records for vans costs nothing and protects you.</p><h3>Related guides</h3><ul><li><a href=\"/pages/fleet-vehicle-inspection-checklist-uk.html\">Fleet vehicle inspection checklist</a></li><li><a href=\"/pages/van-defect-report-uk.html\">Van defect report template</a></li><li><a href=\"/pages/dvsa-walkaround-check-free-template-uk.html\">DVSA walkaround check template</a></li></ul>"
